Bug 2030007 - Save the CardDAV password once the server has accepted it. r=edicharry

The credentials were saved only after the response had been checked against
the statuses the request expected, so a server that authenticated the user
and then refused the request for an unrelated reason left nothing in the
password manager. Necko's auth cache kept the session going, so this showed
up only after a restart.

A failed authentication rejects in CardDAVUtils.makeRequest, so reaching the
save means the server accepted the credentials.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326199

diff --git a/mailnews/addrbook/modules/CardDAVDirectory.sys.mjs b/mailnews/addrbook/modules/CardDAVDirectory.sys.mjs
--- a/mailnews/addrbook/modules/CardDAVDirectory.sys.mjs
+++ b/mailnews/addrbook/modules/CardDAVDirectory.sys.mjs
@@ -249,8 +249,14 @@ export class CardDAVDirectory extends SQ
         "addrbook-directory-request-end",
         this.UID
       );
     }
+    if (callbacks.shouldSaveAuth) {
+      // Save before checking the status: a 401 rejects in makeRequest.
+      this.setStringValue("carddav.username", callbacks.authInfo?.username);
+      await callbacks.saveAuth();
+    }
+
     if (
       details.expectedStatuses &&
       !details.expectedStatuses.includes(response.status)
     ) {
@@ -259,13 +265,8 @@ export class CardDAVDirectory extends SQ
         Cr.NS_ERROR_FAILURE
       );
     }
 
-    if (callbacks.shouldSaveAuth) {
-      // The user was prompted for a username and password. Save the response.
-      this.setStringValue("carddav.username", callbacks.authInfo?.username);
-      await callbacks.saveAuth();
-    }
     return response;
   }
 
